    {
      "text": "None of the driver-side exonerations is available on this record, and I do not assert one. There is no traffic advisory covering the trip window: the only advisory artifact, EV-ADVIS-00106-01, is MISSING, carries weight 0.0 and fired issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, so POL-RD-03 cannot be run. The chat log holds a single rider message with waypoint_hint null and no instruction of any kind, so POL-RD-04 is unavailable and its corroboration test cannot be met. Both amendment timestamps and both amended optimal fields on the trip record are null, so POL-RD-05 does not apply. The vehicle is RYDE_TAXI, not a pooled product, so POL-RD-12 does not apply. The fare model is METERED, not UPFRONT_QUOTE, so POL-RD-11 does not apply. The deviation therefore stands on the booked optimal route of 7.2 km and 19.0 minutes, and the remedy is the POL-RD-02 arithmetic and nothing more.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00106-01", "EV-CHAT-00106", "EV-TRIP-00106", "EV-FARE-00106"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-05", "POL-RD-11", "POL-RD-12"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Both CTE gantry charges are matched to the vehicle's own trace: the nearest fix to the Braddell Rd gantry sits at 0.0 m and the nearest fix to the Chin Swee tunnel gantry at 24.1 m, both far inside the 250 m match radius POL-RD-09(4) uses. The vehicle genuinely crossed both, so neither the $3.00 nor the $2.50 line is a phantom gantry and no standalone billing-integrity refund is due under POL-RD-09(4). Because the deviation is refunded under POL-RD-02, which recomputes the fare including only on-optimal-route gantries (here 0.00), the $5.50 of off-route ERP is already comprehended in that refund and must not be added on top of it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00106", "EV-GPS-00106"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.erp_gantry_proximity.lines",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The recomputation is arithmetic and it caps the driver's exposure: ((3.80 + 0.75 x 7.2 km + 0.28 x 19.0 min) x the surge multiplier of 1.0 read from the fare_breakdown) + 0.80 platform fee + 0.00 on-optimal-route ERP = 15.32, so the refund is 26.04 - 15.32 = 10.72, rounded up to SGD 10.75. That is 41.17% of charged_total, far below the 90% share that would convert the outcome into a FULL_REFUND, and it is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor. The correct outcome on the driver's side of this case is a PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 10.75 and not a cent more.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00106", "EV-TRIP-00106"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing on this record triggers a mandatory escalation or a conduct referral, so the case should be ruled rather than held. The trace is unbroken: 169 fixes at a 10 second sampling interval, 100% coverage, no gaps, a maximum gap of 0.0 seconds, so it is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c) and POL-RD-10(3) does not bite. The driver's trailing-window record shows deviation_flags_90d of 0 against completed_trips_90d of 96, so no repeat-deviation pattern is established under POL-RD-06 and no conduct referral follows. The trip identifiers and timestamps match across the trip record, the trace and the fare breakdown, and the refund is far below the SGD 150.00 ceiling, so no POL-RD-10(1) to (8) trigger fires.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00106", "EV-DPROF-00106", "EV-TRIP-00106", "EV-FARE-00106"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-10", "POL-RD-06"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver asserts no external traffic cause, and no party has cited an advisory for this trip. The absence of any advisory in the bundle (EV-ADVIS-00106-01, MISSING, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT) is a gap in the evidence rather than a contradiction within it. It is therefore not the POL-RD-10(5) situation of an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, and the case is decided on the trace and the remaining clauses rather than escalated.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00106-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-13", "POL-RD-10"]
    }
  ]
}

