    "explanation": "Rider and Driver, I have decided this as a PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 10.75 to the Rider. The governing GPS trace (EV-GPS-00106) measures 10.78 km against the booked optimal distance of 7.2 km (EV-TRIP-00106): an excess of 3.58 km, or 49.72% of optimal. That clears the POL-RD-01 establishment tests because it is over 0.8 km and over 20%, but it does not reach the materiality tests because it is not over 50% and not over 8.0 km. No POL-RD-06 uplift or driver-conduct referral therefore arises. No exculpatory clause applies: the traffic advisory artifact EV-ADVIS-00106-01 is MISSING with weight 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, so POL-RD-03 cannot run; the single chat message is a complaint rather than an instruction and waypoint_hint is null, so POL-RD-04 does not apply; there is no pickup or dropoff amendment; the vehicle is RYDE_TAXI, not pooled; and the fare model is METERED. Under POL-RD-02 I recompute the fare as ((3.80 + 0.75 x 7.2 km + 0.28 x 19.0 min) x 1.0 surge) + 0.80 platform fee + 0.00 on-optimal-route ERP = SGD 15.32. The refund is 26.04 - 15.32 = 10.72, rounded UP to SGD 10.75. That is about 41% of the charged total, below the 90% full-refund share and above the SGD 0.50 de minimis. The 5.50 of off-route ERP is already comprehended in the 10.72 under POL-RD-09(1) and must not be added on top; both CTE gantry charges are matched by the trace within the 250 m radius, so there is no phantom-gantry billing-integrity referral. The trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07(a)-(c), the trip identifiers match across trip record, GPS trace and fare breakdown, and the refund is far below the escalation ceiling, so this case is ruled rather than escalated. The deciding artifacts each carry weight_multiplier 1.0, so confidence is 0.95."
