ither lies on the optimal route; they are itemised here for transparency only under POL-RD-09(1). The driver's request that the case be ruled rather than held is granted: the trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07(a)-(c) (169 fixes, 10 s interval, empty gaps), the trip identifiers match across trip record, trace and fare breakdown, and the refund is far under the SGD 150 ceiling, so no POL-RD-10 trigger fires. The rider's opening ask of the full $26.04 is more than the policy provides — the detour is established but not material, and the recovery is the recomputed-fare difference, through which the $5.50 ERP relief is delivered, not the whole fare. No repeat-deviation pattern arises (deviation_flags_90d 0 of 96 completed trips), so no POL-RD-06 conduct referral follows. Every deciding fact is carried by artifacts at weight 1.0, so confidence is not discounted."
